In this interview, product expert Lenny Rachitsky hosts Hamel Husain and Shreya Shankar to demystify the emerging discipline of evals, a systematic approach to measuring and improving AI application quality. The discussion frames evals as high-ROI data analytics for LLMs, moving beyond unreliable "vibe checks" to a structured workflow involving error analysis and the identification of specific failure modes. A central theme is the importance of open coding, where a domain expert—the "benevolent dictator"—manually reviews traces to uncover jankiness and hallucinations that automated tools often miss. Ultimately, the guests argue that evals function as living PRDs, utilizing LLM-as-a-judge prompts to create a continuous feedback loop that ensures AI products align with user expectations and business goals.